Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 03:11:47 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] V2i: general polynomial marginal Gram entries J_T[G_{a,l},
 G_{b,m}] (21st pair)

For G_{a,l} = (L - P1)^a P_l: inner_genFun expands the inner integral over
sub-multisets of l and powers of L - S; piece_mono_n turns every monomial
weight against U^m (L-S)^n into a moment pieceMn; piece_place integrates
products of power sums by induction over the factors (merge into an open
coordinate, or open one of class c with multiplicity n_c - #open), which
replaces the explicit set-partition count. genEntry_eq gives every entry in
closed form for every N; jT_gen_table3 makes every B21 entry at Table 3 an
explicit rational. Certified: J_T[P4,1], J_T[P_(2,2),1], J_T[L-P1,1], and
J_T[P2,P2] through the general form (equal to V2h), reusing V2h's moment
tables through tableFn_eq (14 row files, 798 piece lemmas).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
